From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:47:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/25] Act on an alert from the alert: skip the seller, pause
 the search

The two things people want to do right after reading a notification are
"never show me this seller again" and "enough of this search for tonight",
and both meant opening the dashboard from a phone. Each Telegram alert now
has a second row of buttons for exactly those, handled by the bot already
running for pairing and /status. A /resume <id> command undoes the pause,
and /status now shows search ids so the argument is easy to find.

Buttons are only honoured from a chat that is a paired destination: anyone
who can see an alert can see the button, which is not the same as anyone
being allowed to press it. Callback data stays inside Telegram's 64-byte
limit; a seller name too long to fit simply loses its button.

Repo.block_seller() appends to the skip list added in the previous change,
case-insensitively and idempotently.
